"B<[[deprecated]] double drem(double >I<x>B<, double >I<y>B<);>\n"
"B<[[deprecated]] float dremf(float >I<x>B<, float >I<y>B<);>\n"
"B<[[deprecated]] long double dreml(long double >I<x>B<, long double "
">I<y>B<);>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:34
msgid "B<remainder>():"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:44
msgid "B<remainderf>(), B<remainderl>():"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:53
msgid "B<drem>(), B<dremf>(), B<dreml>():"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:75
msgid ""
"These functions compute the remainder of dividing I<x> by I<y>.  The return "
"value is I<x-n*y>, where I<n> is the value I<x\\ /\\ y>, rounded to the "
"nearest integer.  If the absolute value of I<x-n*y> is 0.5, I<n> is chosen "
"to be even."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:78
msgid ""
"These functions are unaffected by the current rounding mode (see "
"B<fenv>(3))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:82
msgid "The B<drem>()  function does precisely the same thing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/remainder.3:88
msgid ""
"On success, these functions return the floating-point remainder, I<x-n*y>.  "
"If the return value is 0, it has the sign of I<x>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
